\[2x + 3y + z = 8,\]
\[4x + 4y + 4z = 12,\]
\[x + y + 8z = 10,\]

First, calculate the determinant \(D\):

\[D = \begin{vmatrix}
2 & 3 & 1 \\
4 & 4 & 4 \\
1 & 1 & 8 \\
\end{vmatrix} = 2\begin{vmatrix} 4 & 4 \\ 1 & 8 \end{vmatrix} - 3\begin{vmatrix} 4 & 4 \\ 1 & 8 \end{vmatrix} + 1\begin{vmatrix} 4 & 4 \\ 1 & 1 \end{vmatrix}\]
\[= 2((4*8) - (4*1)) - 3((4*8) - (4*1)) + ((4*1) - (4*1))\]
\[= 2(32 - 4) - 3(32 - 4) + (4 - 4)\]
\[= 2(28) - 3(28) + 0\]
\[= 56 - 84\]
\[= -28.\]

Next, calculate \(D_x\):

\[D_x = \begin{vmatrix}
8 & 3 & 1 \\
12 & 4 & 4 \\
10 & 1 & 8 \\
\end{vmatrix} = 8\begin{vmatrix} 4 & 4 \\ 1 & 8 \end{vmatrix} - 3\begin{vmatrix} 12 & 4 \\ 10 & 8 \end{vmatrix} + 1\begin{vmatrix} 12 & 4 \\ 10 & 1 \end{vmatrix}\]
\[= 8(32 - 4) - 3(96 - 40) + (12 - 40)\]
\[= 8(28) - 3(56) - 28\]
\[= 224 - 168 - 28\]
\[= 28.\]

Then, calculate \(D_y\):

\[D_y = \begin{vmatrix}
2 & 8 & 1 \\
4 & 12 & 4 \\
1 & 10 & 8 \\
\end{vmatrix} = 2\begin{vmatrix} 12 & 4 \\ 10 & 8 \end{vmatrix} - 8\begin{vmatrix} 4 & 4 \\ 1 & 8 \end{vmatrix} + 1\begin{vmatrix} 4 & 12 \\ 1 & 10 \end{vmatrix}\]
\[= 2(96 - 40) - 8(32 - 4) + (40 - 12)\]
\[= 2(56) - 8(28) + 28\]
\[= 112 - 224 + 28\]
\[= -84.\]

Finally, calculate \(D_z\):

\[D_z = \begin{vmatrix}
2 & 3 & 8 \\
4 & 4 & 12 \\
1 & 1 & 10 \\
\end{vmatrix} = 2\begin{vmatrix} 4 & 12 \\ 1 & 10 \end{vmatrix} - 3\begin{vmatrix} 4 & 12 \\ 1 & 10 \end{vmatrix} + 8\begin{vmatrix} 4 & 4 \\ 1 & 1 \end{vmatrix}\]
\[= 2(40 - 12) - 3(40 - 12) + 8(4 - 4)\]
\[= 2(28) - 3(28) + 0\]
\[= 56 - 84\]
\[= -28.\]

Now, we can find \(x, y, z\):

\[x = \frac{D_x}{D} = \frac{28}{-28} = -1,\]
\[y = \frac{D_y}{D} = \frac{-84}{-28} = 3,\]
\[z = \frac{D_z}{D} = \frac{-28}{-28} = 1.\]

Therefore, the solution is \([-1, 3, 1]\), which corresponds to option D.
